  "meta": {
    "space": "embeddings_ability.npy",
    "projection": "classical MDS + SMACOF, canonically oriented",
    "clustering": "average-linkage agglomerative on cosine distance, 2 levels",
    "cards": 95,
    "unresolved": [],
    "note": "Positions are LOCAL to this deck and are not atlas positions — the deck is re-laid-out from its own cards, which is the whole point. Anything that draws this must say so.",
    "named_by": "deck-cartographer",
    "cartographer_notes": [
      "The rebuild's thesis is not on the record yet. THE HOARD holds 14 cards and exactly two verified ones - Old Gnawbone and Savage Ventmaw, both pre-rebuild Aggravated Assault pieces. Not one of the new Treasure cards (Smaug, The Misty Mountains Cold, Tireless Provisioner, Magda, Professional Face-Breaker, Swashbuckler Extraordinaire) carries a verified flag. The map shows a new engine; the stacks still describe the old one.",
      "Nine of the deck's thirteen verified cards sit in city-2, six of them in BURN ON ARRIVAL. That neighbourhood is the engine on the record, and it is the damage half of the deck rather than the Treasure half.",
      "Aggravated Assault is the hub of all three contained two-card infinites, and it clusters into ANSWERS AND SHORTCUTS - not with the mana Dragons it loops with. That is the map working as designed: it groups by what a card SAYS, and Assault says 'extra combat phase'. Do not read the distance between city-2 and city-3 as the loop being far away.",
      "Reckless Fireweaver is one of the five Treasure sinks and it lives in BURN ON ARRIVAL, across town from THE HOARD, because its text is damage rather than mana. Worth knowing before any department says the sinks are all in one place.",
      "Savage Lands is the only land outside city-1 - it sits in ANSWERS AND SHORTCUTS. A stray, not a finding: 30 of the deck's 31 land entries cluster together and this one landed a city over. Membership left exactly as measured.",
      "Blasphemous Act is the odd member of THE DRAGON DISCOUNT: it is there because it also reads 'costs {1} less', and it is the only card in that neighbourhood that is a sweeper rather than a discount. The split still reads clean, and the shared text is a real thing about the card.",
      "Miirym, Sentinel Wyrm is the only creature in THE INSURANCE. It belongs: ward and token copies are resilience bought at cast time rather than held up, which is the same job the instants do a turn later.",
      "city-2-hood-1 (Counterspell, Dovin's Veto, Swan Song) sits at cy 0.94 against its city's centroid of 0.28 - the most detached lobe on the map. Three blue instants in a deck whose blue is a splash. That is the deck's most unusual pocket, and it reads as deliberate rather than misfiled.",
      "city-4, city-5 and city-6 each carry a single neighbourhood identical to the city, so no neighbourhood name is supplied for them - the deterministic fallback is honest there.",
      "city-1 is 30 of 95 mapped entries, the largest mass on the map, and all of it is land. In a five-colour deck at bracket 4 that is not padding; it is the price of the other six cities being castable."
    ]
  },
